//- 7:20 THE DENOUEMENT and the closer, then the end of the yes path at 7:50. Pays off the opener's "what does that say about us?" and Webb's spaceship, out loud over the deep field.

section.over-media(data-background-image="img/deep-field.jpg" data-timing="20")
  h2 You'll never see what someone else sees.
  cite.credit NASA, ESA, CSA, STScI
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Webb's first deep field. Nearly every speck is a galaxy.
      li We share some words and some concepts, but no actual truth. Everyone you meet is in their own spaceship, with their own sensors. You can connect, but you'll never see what they see.
      li And that's beautiful. It means people can surprise you.
      li It means empathy is the most valuable thing you have.

//- The closer: the room is at a party, so send them to it. The call to action is a subhead, one size up from a caption's.
section.over-media.has-subhead(data-background-image="img/holi.jpg" data-timing="10")
  h2 You're at a party.
  p.fragment Go ask someone what they see.
  cite.credit Photo: KuldeepRawat07
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Holi, in Nandgaon. The festival of colors.
      li Click: go ask someone what they see. You'll never know for sure, and that's the fun.

//- The end: just the lemon, centred, and the address small in mono near the bottom.
